 succeeded in 617ms:
of several wrong implementations. Not measured, no witness built; the rung-3 attempt is owed.

### `xscaleinten` (HIGH) -- filed 2026-09-10

`cpu_arm_coproc.c`, grep anchor `void arm_coproc_i80321_6`, crm 0 / crn 0: the load arm reads

```c
cpu->cd.arm.r[rd] = cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten;
fatal("TODO: XScale read from inten?\n");
exit(1);
```

The destination register receives the modelled value and the process then dies. The store arm immediately
below writes the same field and the i80321 interrupt controller consumes it, so the register is fully
modelled both ways.

*** THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE IS THE SIBLING CASE IN THE SAME SWITCH, one screen away. *** `case 4:`
(`i80321_isteer`) has the **identical structure** -- load arm assigns from the modelled field, store arm
writes it -- and carries **no `fatal()` and no `exit()`**. So `crn 0`'s kill is an OUTLIER inside its own
switch rather than a policy: the upstream-residue pattern this project has now found several times, where
the author hit the exit he happened to reach while developing and not the sibling he did not. *That is a
far stronger warrant than "it is a host kill", and it is one grep away* -- which is exactly what the
option-set rule's sibling check is for.

Reachability is explicit rather than inferred: `machine_iq80321.c` installs it with
`cpu->cd.arm.coproc[6] = arm_coproc_i80321_6;`, and Iyonix does the same. Emulated firmware reading its
own interrupt-enable register is the natural consumer, and the generic coprocessor dispatcher enforces no
supervisor-only precondition.

Disposition: **member 4 (ACCEPT)**, two lines deleted, no latch, for the same reason as `mapledmaaddr`.
FAULT is unavailable regardless -- the failed-device exception path is MIPS and M88K only, and this is
ARM. Not measured, no witness built. Note the witness needs a **coprocessor read from an ARM guest**,
which is a different vehicle from the device probes this project mostly writes; `gate_arm.sh`'s decode
checks are the nearest existing machinery.

*Both rows came from the GPT-6 Astra exit audit's top three (`regress/artifacts/queuetriage/`), which
ranked them I1/E1 out of 76 unowned runtime error-exit sites across 24 files. Every element above was
re-derived locally by opening the files.*

### `crimewidthkill` (HIGH) -- filed 2026-09-10

`dev_sgi_ip32.c`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(crime)`, grep anchor `fatal("crime access len = %i!\n", len);`: the
handler is a bare `if (len == 8) {...} else if (len == 4) {...} else { fatal(...); exit(1); }`. There is
no other width arm, so **every other access length -- 1, 2, and anything wider -- ends the emulator.** A
byte load is an ordinary thing for a guest or a PROM to do while probing, and nothing about the device's
mapping advertises a width restriction.

`machine_sgi.c` installs it with `dev_crime_init(machine, mem, 0x14000000, ...)` on the IP32 machines.
CRIME is the memory and interrupt controller: one of the first things any IP32 guest touches.

**The disposition is the interesting part, because member 5 (FAULT) is genuinely available here, which it
usually is not.** `memory_rw.c` converts a failed device callback into an architectural access exception
for **MIPS and M88K only** -- and this device is on MIPS. So `return 0` is not a silent decline: it is a
positive statement that the access could not be serviced, delivered as the bus error real hardware gives.
That is the `dev_unreadable.c` idiom, and `machine_sgi.c` already installs `dev_unreadable` ten times for
exactly this reason -- the PROM and NetBSD probe absent regions and RELY on the failure. A round here
should weigh FAULT against DECLINE rather than defaulting to decline as most of this queue does. Not
measured, no witness; the rung-3 attempt is owed and looks cheap.

### `vmedefaultkill` (HIGH) -- filed 2026-09-10

`dev_vme.c`, default arm: it announces with **`debug()`** and then calls `exit(1)`.

*** THIS ONE IS WORSE THAN THE USUAL SHAPE, AND THE REASON IS THE DIAGNOSTIC LEVEL. *** Every other
unimplemented-register kill in this queue announces with `fatal()`, which this fork has measured cannot be
silenced by `-q` -- `fatal()` has no early-out and goes straight to `va_debug`. This one uses `debug()`,
which does have one (`if ((quiet_mode && !ss) || v < 0) return;`), so at default verbosity **the message
is not printed at all and the emulator dies with no output explaining why.** A user sees the process
vanish; a gate sees a non-zero exit and no diagnostic to grep. That makes it the hardest member of the
class to DIAGNOSE, independent of how hard it is to trigger.

`machine_mvme88k.c` installs it unconditionally (`vme addr=...`, `VME2_BASE`) on a machine this project
actively boots -- the same constructor attaches the PCC2 the recent rounds are about. Probing a bus
controller's register space is exactly what firmware does.

Disposition: member 5 (FAULT) is **available** -- M88K is one of the two families `memory_rw.c` delivers a
failed-device exception for -- so `return 0` gives the guest the bus error real VME hardware would. Member
3 is the alternative and would need the announce **promoted from `debug()` to `fatal()`** to be worth
anything, which is a second change the round must make deliberately rather than inherit.

### `fbctrlportkill` (HIGH) -- filed 2026-09-10

`dev_fbctrl.c`: **the PORT arm accepts an out-of-range port number with a warning and STORES it, and the
  `is_userpage` (MMU-on). [#382 correction: `is_userpage` is set by the
  LDRT/STRT T-bit alone and is reachable MMU-off �?" the divergence is NOT gated
  on the MMU being enabled; see the #382 round block.] The LDM-with-PC instrument gap (no probe row loads
  PC through the multi path, so the round's headline severity is source-read,
  not measured) was merged into task #59.

## One-hundred-and-nineteenth round (#378) �?" a BE guest's every LDM/STM through a warm page was byte-reversed, 23 handlers of it into PC

`generate_arm_multi.c` emits the LDM/STM fast path as raw host-word moves �?" no
byte-order term anywhere in the generator �?" while the `bdt_load`/`bdt_store`
fallback (via `arm_pop`/`arm_push`) swaps on both its warm and cold arms. The
dispatcher installed the fast path with no `cpu->byte_order` test, so on this
LE host a big-endian guest's multi-transfers to a WARM page moved reversed
words and to a COLD page correct ones �?" `#372`'s self-contradiction class with
the **polarity inverted** (there the general path was wrong; here the fast
path). Not just data: **23 of the 256 emitted handlers load PC**, so a BE
`ldm {...,pc}` function return jumped to a byte-reversed address. LDM/STM sits
on every prologue/epilogue, making this the largest ARM-BE defect to date.

- **#378 (`cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c`)** �?" one line: the fast-path install gate now
  also requires `cpu->byte_order == EMUL_LITTLE_ENDIAN`, so a BE guest takes
  the already-correct `bdt_*` everywhere. Resolving the guest term at
  TRANSLATE time is sound because `byte_order` cannot change afterwards, a
  fact three review seats verified independently by exhausting the routes: the
  CP15 c1 B-bit write calls `fatal()` and **exits** (now commented as
  load-bearing in `cpu_arm_coproc.c` �?" a future endian-switch round needs
  translation-cache invalidation AND re-translation, since instruction decode
  reads `byte_order` too); SETEND is undecoded and `ARM_FLAG_E` inert; every
  host-side write is machine-setup-time. Closing the gate also closes the
  `netbsd_memcpy` fold's raw `pw[]` publishes **for free** �?" its matcher
  requires the fast-path handler installed, so it declines on BE (the `#354`
  invariant comment is amended to say so) �?" and disables the order-immune
  memset fold on BE (a performance note, not a correctness change).
- **#378 (`regress/arm_endian_probe.py`, rewritten)** �?" 12 �+' 34 rows with
  EXPLICIT per-row kinds: `#372`'s DISC rows are the COLD ones, `#378`'s are
  the WARM ones, and the old "cold in name ��' DISC" expression would have
  labelled the new rows backwards. New: warm/cold STM byte-witness ladders,
  warm/cold LDM word rows with zero sentinels, LE invariance mirrors, and a
  second liveness control (`ENDIAN_CONTROL378`: the cold multi rows go through
  `bdt_*` on every build, so they prove the machinery live independent of fix
  state). Grouped spawns; explicit `put` width on every command (`put_type` is
  static and sticky); r10/r11 read as `sl`/`fp` (the debugger has no rN
  spelling for them). All 18 new words unassemble-verified WITH REGISTERS.
