None of the other seven has the same warranted two-line ACCEPT fix as `xscaleinten`. The steering field has no routing consumer, the source-status field is shared with the interrupt controller, and PID is unused by address translation. Preserving those assignments would not implement the requested behavior.

The existing gate already checks undefined-exception handler output, mode, and return address. That gives the top two fixes a useful detector pattern, though they still need a session on a machine that installs these handlers.

